  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 923 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nThe main talking point in the long term forecast will be monitoring\nan upper level trough and subsequent sfc low pushing into the\nTennessee Valley from the southwest on Friday. Current model guidance\nindicates strong disagreement in whether or not the area of low\npressure shifts northward enough to allow mentionable rain chances in\nour area. Therefore, due to low confidence in this system's\ninfluence, have continued with blended guidance for this weekend.\nTherefore, very low rain chances (less than 15%) are forecast Friday\nthrough Sunday. Temperatures during this time will be dependent on \nhow much cloud cover filters in from the aforementioned system, so \ndid not make any changes to the blended guidance output. Highs during\nthis time are forecast to warm into the upper 60s to lower 70s with \novernight lows dropping into the upper 40s to lower 50s. If you have\noutdoor interests this weekend, check back in for an update later in\nthe work week as confidence grows in the track of the low pressure\nsystem.",
